cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the designs or the engine from antivenom-mrna, please cite it
  and say which version you used. The designs are in-silico: no therapeutic
  efficacy is demonstrated, and this is not medical advice.
title: antivenom-mrna
authors:
  - alias: sanjibani
    website: 'https://github.com/sanjibani'
version: 0.5.0
date-released: '2026-11-01'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/sanjibani/antivenom-mrna'
abstract: >-
  Open, reproducible, full-construct mRNA designs for India's Big Four
  venomous snakes, and the auditable design engine that produced them. The
  engine measures licensed mRNA vaccines, optimises coding sequences,
  assembles full constructs from cap to poly(A), and plans antibody
  cocktails by exact set cover over a literature map of published
  neutralising candidates. Every sequence carries a provenance record and a
  checksum; every report is generated by the code it describes.
keywords:
  - mRNA
  - antivenom
  - snakebite
  - codon optimisation
  - synthetic biology
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
